#: manual/design/autodiff.md:3
msgid "This page explains why the root package `Luna-Flow/autodiff` is a pure re-export facade and how its surface was chosen."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:6
#: manual/design/checked.md:7
#: manual/design/core.md:6
#: manual/design/dual.md:8
#: manual/design/elementary.md:6
#: manual/design/forward.md:7
#: manual/design/linalg.md:7
#: manual/design/poly.md:7
msgid "Design goal"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:8
msgid "One import should be enough to differentiate scalar code: the number type, the drivers, and every trait that appears in the bounds of `Dual[T]`. At the same time no behaviour may live in two places, so that the root package can never disagree with `dual` and `forward`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:13
#: manual/design/checked.md:13
#: manual/design/core.md:12
#: manual/design/dual.md:16
#: manual/design/elementary.md:12
#: manual/design/forward.md:13
#: manual/design/linalg.md:13
#: manual/design/poly.md:13
msgid "Mathematical background"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:15
msgid "The root package adds no mathematics. Its content is the vocabulary of the [dual design](dual.md): the commutative ring $T[\\varepsilon]/(\\varepsilon^2)$ needs the structure traits `Zero`, `One`, `AddMonoid`, `AddGroup`, `MulMonoid`, `Semiring` and `Ring`; the elementary rules $f(a + b\\varepsilon) = f(a) + f'(a)\\,b\\,\\varepsilon$ need `Sqrt`, `Exponential`, `Logarithmic` and `Trigonometric` on `T` and the canonical map $\\mathbb Z \\to T$ (`IntegralHomomorphism`); the checked rules need `DivChecked`, `SqrtChecked` and the context and error values; and `Constants` provides $\\pi$, $\\tau$ and $e$ as dual constants."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:25
#: manual/design/checked.md:45
#: manual/design/core.md:35
#: manual/design/dual.md:142
#: manual/design/elementary.md:35
#: manual/design/forward.md:56
#: manual/design/linalg.md:62
#: manual/design/poly.md:59
msgid "Design decisions"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:27
msgid "Re-export with `pub using`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:29
msgid "**Problem.** Users of `Dual[T]` write bounds such as `T : Ring + Trigonometric`, which name traits from two other modules."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:32
msgid "**Options.** Ask users to import `luna-generic` and `arithmetic` themselves; define local traits; re-export."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:35
msgid "**Choice.** `pub using` re-exports in [`src/alias.mbt`](../../../src/alias.mbt). A re-exported name is the original trait or type, so instances written against `@lg.Ring` or `@arithmetic.Sqrt` work with `@autodiff.Ring` and `@autodiff.Sqrt`, and no second trait hierarchy exists. Defining local traits would split the ecosystem and break instance sharing."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:42
msgid "Exactly the bounds of `Dual[T]`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:44
msgid "The root package re-exports the traits that occur in the bounds of the public `Dual` methods and instances, plus the error and context types of the checked methods. It does not re-export `Field`, `MulGroup` or `Inverse` (which `Dual[T]` deliberately lacks), nor `NatHomomorphism` (only needed by a deprecated method form), nor the contextual or enclosure traits of `arithmetic`, which `Dual[T]` does not implement."
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:51
msgid "Drivers but no bridges"
msgstr ""

#: manual/design/autodiff.md:53
msgid "`diff` and `value_and_diff` are re-exported because they only need `dual`. The `linalg` and `poly` drivers are not, because re-exporting them would make every user of the root package depend on `linear-algebra` and `luna-poly`."
msgstr ""

